  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "First touch out to the side",
  "description": "Set up a cone gate on each side of the receiver B, with a line of A players a little way in front. A passes to B, who receives and steers the ball out through one of the gates with the same touch – control and direction in one. B then dribbles back and joins the end of the line, and A steps up to be the receiver.\n\nProgression: A follows the pass and presses. B uses the first touch and a feint to get out either way. With lots of players, run several stations side by side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look both ways before the ball arrives – what do you need to know before you pick a direction?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Open your body towards the way you want to go before you receive."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Control and direction is one touch – don't stop the ball first."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
